# build output
dist/
# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# environment variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# host CLIs
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/

# Claude Code — local tooling, deliberately not published. CLAUDE.md and the
# skills/agents under .claude/ are how the site is worked on, not part of what
# it is. Contribution is recorded in the commit trailer instead.
#
# NOTE: like the personal files below, these now live on one machine only.
# CLAUDE.md holds design decisions that the source comments summarise but do
# not fully replace — keep a copy off this disk.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# VS Code, as an allowlist rather than a blocklist. extensions.json and
# launch.json describe the PROJECT — which extension to install, how to start
# the dev server — so they belong to anyone who clones it. Everything else in
# here is personal or worse: settings.json collects individual preferences,
# and sftp.json / ftp-sync.json are a well-known way people commit deployment
# credentials by accident. Listing what is allowed means a file nobody
# anticipated is excluded by default.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json

# personal, local-only files — source material and working notes, not part of
# the published site or the public repo. RESUME.md carries a phone number and
# an email in plain text; WEBSITE-CONTEXT.md names clients that must never
# appear on the site. The résumé the site actually links to is
# public/resume.pdf, which is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# NOTE: being ignored means these exist on one machine only and are not backed
# up by pushing. Keep a copy somewhere else.
RESUME.md
RUN.md
WEBSITE-CONTEXT.md

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
